# ==============================================================================
# CURRENT STATE (verified against src/supabaseClient.js, August 2026):
# This app does NOT currently read any environment variables. The Supabase
# project URL and public key are hardcoded directly in src/supabaseClient.js.
# Nothing needs to be set here for the app to run — `npm install && npm run dev`
# works with zero .env file present.
#
# The previous version of this file referenced GEMINI_API_KEY and APP_URL.
# Those were leftovers from this project's original Google AI Studio scaffold
# and the @google/genai package that used them was already removed from
# package.json. Nothing in the current codebase reads either variable —
# they have been removed from this file as inaccurate.
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# RECOMMENDED (not yet implemented — requires a small code change first):
# Moving Supabase config from hardcoded values in src/supabaseClient.js to
# environment variables would let a new owner point this app at their own
# Supabase project without editing source code. If that change is made,
# these are the standard Vite-convention variable names to use (Vite only
# exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code):
# ==============================================================================

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLIC_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here
